{
  "rationale": "The plant automaton G1 models the robot's perception and motion capabilities, separating perception (sensor events) and motion (controllable actions) into a single automaton for clarity. The specification automaton E1 enforces conservative exploration: random_walk is used in clear states, move_forward is only allowed in a dedicated commit state, and obstacle events force immediate turn-based recovery. Obstacle recovery states only allow the appropriate rotation, and after recovery, the robot returns to exploration. This ensures steady progress, reliable collision avoidance, and no infinite controllable loops.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate clear, commit, and recovery states to enforce conservative obstacle handling and steady progress.",
    "Allow only one controllable action per non-terminal state, with random_walk as the default in clear, move_forward in commit, and rotation in recovery."
  ],
